WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your partner in crime
on this show, Nick Offerman,

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously your co-star
in "Parks and Rec."

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've known him
for a long time, though.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:05.939 line:92%
-Yeah, we met in Chicago.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met at a really weird
house party.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:12.946
And Nick was in a production of
"Clockwork Orange."

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:15.081 line:92%
And he had a dyed red beard

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his hair was shaped into
devil horns.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you saw that and thought
that was interesting?

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was like, "My man."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:26.960
But that was during a time when
if you remember in Chicago,

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was some factions.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because there were
the improvisers and the sketch

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
and -- like, you know,
stand-up's kind of

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the same group.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the Goodman Theatre,
Steppenwolf,

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.872
like, professional actors.
-Yeah. Actor actors. Yeah.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:42.876
-And then the alternative
theater Chicago actors,

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.777 line:92%
of which I think Nick was one.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.179
So everybody -- they didn't run
in the same circles.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:49.382
-Did you have any -- did you
feel any crossover comfort

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.116 line:92%
with those other circles?

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.685 size:88% position:44%
-I felt like I could do
everything they could do

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they couldn't do
what I could do.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that bad to say out loud?
-No, no, that's good.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay. But no.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.461
They were amazing and I never --
you know, I never --

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
I never went
to Steppenwolf or --

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.130 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Did you go to any --

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I went to
like three Steppenwolf shows

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.934 line:92%
the entire time I was there.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:08.468 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, I --

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say they were --
it was expensive.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was expensive.
-Yeah.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.906
-But it was like Laurie Metcalf
and Gary Sinise,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
all these amazing actors
that were there.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But we were...

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were just, like,
scraping it by.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were just throwing hot dog
buns into the audience.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:22.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:23.516 line:92%
In some basement theater.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously Nick is sort of
famously good

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
at building things.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.121 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And he's a craftsman.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:28.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are not.
-No.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Does he take advantage of --
on the show,

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.559
of the fact that you know
very little about crafting?

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:35.695
-Yeah. He could say pretty much
anything and he would just --

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would just nod.
-Yeah.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As if I know what it --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, there is a couple times
in it that,

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:42.402
it was kind of like a little bit
of a living stress dream,

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:43.169 size:84% position:42% line:92%
where people would say,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, all you need to do
is just plane this

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:46.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it'll be
in good shape."

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.976
And I would nod as if I knew
what everybody is talking about.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would be afraid
people would ask me to do it.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:56.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, no,
I can't make anything yet.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.317 line:92%
-The show is called "Making It."

00:01:57.317 --> 00:02:00.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys have a catch phrase
that is very inventive.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.990
-What is the catch phrase on the
television show "Making It"?

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Make it!

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
Yeah.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.761
-Did you shop around for others?
-We did.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.529 line:92%
-Or did you immediately --

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We went to -- We went to
a bunch of clubs.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
We tried out a bunch of
catch phrases.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, like stand-up clubs?
-Yeah.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.503
-You did, like, open mikes?
-We did open mike stuff.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
We went on the road.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:18.638 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We worked really hard.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.875
And what was great is we
realized simple is better.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:22.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Always.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.544 line:92%
-Did you have any failed ones?

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:25.078 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-We didn't.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
-We didn't.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:29.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just tried one
and then we stuck with it.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:29.616 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.316 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And then we also --

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
We could never quite say it
at the same time.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.053 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Oh, that was the issue.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just syncing up and saying it
together.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.925
-Do you guys have a slogan here
on your show?

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.093 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-We do have a slogan.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.327 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's also "make it."

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.596 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:46.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Late Night with Seth Meyers"
and make it.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Make it!
-Yeah.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's weird.
-Make it!

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.569 line:92%
-Oh, it's said differently.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.403 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Make it!

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
We try to say it in a way that
they don't know

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:55.441
if we're going to make something
or they're supposed to.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.076 line:92%
-I like that. I like that.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really hard to think of
a catch phrase, you know?

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, to -- and we didn't want
to do something like,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Get out of here, loser."
You know?

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:03.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.218 size:81% position:41%
Well, it's a very --
Well, it's interesting

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you guys are the hosts
of the show.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not judges on the show.
-No.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have to do any of
that tough stuff.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you wish you --
I mean, like --

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will say you are someone
who has opinions about things.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I -- Yes.
-Yeah.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:20.934
-I don't -- I would never want
to -- A creative person who,

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.603
like, is very vulnerable
and puts himself out there,

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:27.307
I would never want to be the one
that says, like, you know,

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.775 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Hasta la vista, baby."

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I would not want
to do that.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:34.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think you could say, like,
"Make it to the door."

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:35.014 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:35.882 line:92%
"Because you outta here."

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Make it your business
to get in the car."

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:39.586 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.386 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"And get out of here."

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:44.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Make a door and then leave
through it."

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.127 line:92%
-But, yeah. You're right.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:51.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very judgmental
and I do like to judge.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:54.367
-But I can see that you wouldn't
take pleasure from, like,

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.101 size:84% position:42% line:92%
judging an artisanal --

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:58.571
-No, I enjoy doing it with you,
like, just the two of us now.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.540
-No one is watching or anything.
-Right.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-But I like that.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.544
But if it was on a, like,
you Know, a TV show --

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah, no.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:05.812 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:06.613 line:92%
Heaven forbid. That's the thing.

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:10.016
That's why I have a TV show, I
try not to be judgmental at all.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:10.984 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you now?
-You were on --

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.455
We had dinner last night
with some of our friends.

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:15.855 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-We did.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you then had to -- you
were, like, kind of

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first one out the door
because you had to do

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:20.526 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the "Today" show.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:24.330
-I did the "Today" show
this morning, which was so fun.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.732 line:92%
And that show is amazing.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.200 line:92%
Like, it's a crazy circus.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-As you know.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:32.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I texted a friend of ours,
because this morning

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:33.172 line:92%
it was like an "SNL" sketch

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.942 size:84% position:42%
that we had probably
written a million times

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.011
because I was a little hungover.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not a lot of sleep, and I had
to get up really early.

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:45.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had to do crafts,
which I don't do.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.754 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-With Al Roker and Hoda.

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:51.324
And I followed a story about
a giraffe getting pregnant.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:51.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.826
But it made me think about,
we used to joke all the time

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.496
that there would always be
sketches where we would think

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.032
it was really funny if it was
like the local newscasters

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Tucson
who were really hung over

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.801 size:81% position:41%
and just trying to get
through the morning.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:02.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:07.140
-They're like, "Good morning,
T-- Good morning, Tucson."

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.941 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just trying not to throw up
the whole time.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.347
Well, I think we may have
even talked about it here.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was like a -- I remember
there was a famous night

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we were out
very late at "SNL."

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:23.189
And then you, Finesse Mitchell
and Kenan Thompson had to leave.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:27.393
Like, you had -- Well, you left
a bar, like, an hour before

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:32.832
you got picked up to all go play
the Black Eyed Peas in a sketch.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that was such
a dark, dark day.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you filmed it
and it was really exciting

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the rest of us because you
then all told us, like,

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:41.874 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"We were so hung over

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we had to dance
like the Black Eyed Peas.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:47.580
And then when we all just got
wait to watch the pre-tape."

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.149
And then it was so much fun
to watch because you guys

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
all looked like really unhappy
Black Eyed Peas.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:53.519 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Kenan Thompson was doing
the funniest bit

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:58.057
where he was pretending to take
calls from himself

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:58.624 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the night before.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like, "Hello?"
And he was like,

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:03.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You want me to go home?
I don't think so."

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:03.930 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was, like, going,
"You got to go home, man.

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.200 line:92%
You're going to be up all night.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.002
And you got to be the
Black Eyed Peas in the morning."

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.003 line:92%
He's like, "Nice try, buddy."

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How about, by the way,
our friend --

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:15.742
Our friend Kenan Thompson
finally got an Emmy nomination.

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:16.242 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So great!

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for Kenan Thompson,
everybody!

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.579 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:23.583
-And still an American citizen,
Kenan. Right?

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:24.851 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yes, still -- no, no.

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:26.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
They took it away for Horatio.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:27.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
-So now he's --

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They had to split --
they switched it.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, makes sense.
That makes sense. Yeah.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that's how it works.
-That's how -- that's the biz.

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:34.127 line:92%
-We don't add one more person!

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:36.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what,
you want to be here?

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:37.864 line:92%
You got to give us someone!

